        "prefix_token_count": 105,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Let \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\). The cross product equation is given by:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 90 \\\\ 30 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 468,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 469,
        "char_start": 258,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 192,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 193,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Compute the cross product on the left side:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2z + 5y \\\\ -5x - z \\\\ x - 2y \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 630,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 631,
        "char_start": 470,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 264,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 265,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Set this equal to the right side vector:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 2z + 5y \\\\ -5x - z \\\\ x - 2y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 90 \\\\ 30 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 728,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 729,
        "char_start": 632,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 317,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 318,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: This gives us three equations:\n\\[\n2z + 5y = 90,\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x - z = 30,\n\\]\n\\[\nx - 2y = 30.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 791,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 792,
        "char_start": 730,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 344,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 345,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Solve the third equation for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 30 + 2y.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 947,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 948,
        "char_start": 793,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 424,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 425,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Substitute \\(x\\) into the second equation:\n\\[\n-5(30 + 2y) - z = 30 \\implies -150 - 10y - z = 30 \\implies -10y - z = 180 \\implies z = -10y - 180.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1120,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1121,
        "char_start": 949,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 517,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 518,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: Substitute \\(z\\) into the first equation:\n\\[\n2(-10y - 180) + 5y = 90 \\implies -20y - 360 + 5y = 90 \\implies -15y - 360 = 90 \\implies -15y = 450 \\implies y = -30.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1251,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1252,
        "char_start": 1122,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 601,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 602,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Find \\(x\\) and \\(z\\) using \\(y = -30\\):\n\\[\nx = 30 + 2(-30) = 30 - 60 = -30,\n\\]\n\\[\nz = -10(-30) - 180 = 300 - 180 = 120.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1368,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1369,
        "char_start": 1253,
        "effective_step": 9,
