  "raw_text": "Step 1: Let \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\). The cross product equation is given by:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 90 \\\\ 30 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nStep 2: Compute the cross product on the left side:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2z + 5y \\\\ -5x - z \\\\ x - 2y \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nStep 3: Set this equal to the right side vector:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 2z + 5y \\\\ -5x - z \\\\ x - 2y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 90 \\\\ 30 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nStep 4: This gives us three equations:\n\\[\n2z + 5y = 90,\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x - z = 30,\n\\]\n\\[\nx - 2y = 30.\n\\]\nStep 5: Solve the third equation for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 30 + 2y.\n\\]\nStep 6: Substitute \\(x\\) into the second equation:\n\\[\n-5(30 + 2y) - z = 30 \\implies -150 - 10y - z = 30 \\implies -10y - z = 180 \\implies z = -10y - 180.\n\\]\nStep 7: Substitute \\(z\\) into the first equation:\n\\[\n2(-10y - 180) + 5y = 90 \\implies -20y - 360 + 5y = 90 \\implies -15y - 360 = 90 \\implies -15y = 450 \\implies y = -30.\n\\]\nStep 8: Find \\(x\\) and \\(z\\) using \\(y = -30\\):\n\\[\nx = 30 + 2(-30) = 30 - 60 = -30,\n\\]\n\\[\nz = -10(-30) - 180 = 300 - 180 = 120.\n\\]\nStep 9: Therefore, the vector \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} -30 \\\\ -30 \\\\ 120 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nStep 10: Calculate the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{v}\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(-30)^2 + (-30)^2 + 120^2} = \\sqrt{900 + 900 + 14400} = \\sqrt{16200} = 30\\sqrt{18} = 90\\sqrt{2}.\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -30 \\\\ -30 \\\\ 120 \\end{pmatrix}}<|im_end|>",
